      "type": "row"
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "title": "DR Drill Overall Status",
      "type": "stat",
      "description": "Plain English: Shows whether our automated cold failover disaster recovery drill passed completely.\n\n\u2022 What is RTO? Recovery Time Objective: The time in seconds taken to restore and boot verified services.\n\u2022 What is RPO? Recovery Point Objective: Data freshness measured by backup archive age.\n\u2022 What should I do if this is red? A red status means the failover drill encountered a database corruption error or container crash. Run 'tools/backup-dr/dr-drill.sh' locally or over SSH to inspect the failure step.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 8
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "victoriametrics"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "0": {
                  "color": "red",
                  "text": "DRILL FAILED"
                },
                "1": {
                  "color": "green",
                  "text": "CLEAN / PASSED"
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "victoriametrics"
          },
          "expr": "selfhosted_dr_drill_status",
          "legendFormat": "Drill Status",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "title": "Backup Execution Status",
      "type": "stat",
      "description": "Plain English: Status of the most recent scheduled backup run per service (1 = Success, 0 = Failure).\n\n\u2022 What is RTO? Recovery Time Objective: The total time needed to recover services from backups.\n\u2022 What is RPO? Recovery Point Objective: The age of the newest backup data.\n\u2022 What should I do if this is red? A red service indicates the backup run failed or cloud upload to B2 was interrupted. Inspect backup-runner logs on bjorn via 'docker logs --tail 100 backup-runner'.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 8
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "victoriametrics"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          "mappings": [
            {
              "type": "value",
              "options": {
                "0": {
                  "color": "red",
                  "text": "FAILED"
                },
                "1": {
                  "color": "green",
                  "text": "OK"
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "orientation": "horizontal",
        "textMode": "auto"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "victoriametrics"
          },
          "expr": "selfhosted_backup_status{service=~\"$service\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{service}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "title": "Service Backup Freshness Gauge",
      "type": "gauge",
      "description": "Plain English: Shows how many hours old the latest backup is for each service. SLA allows up to 26 hours to account for daily backup drift.\n\n\u2022 What is RTO? Recovery Time Objective: Time required to restore full service functionality.\n\u2022 What is RPO? Recovery Point Objective: The maximum data loss window, represented here by archive age.\n\u2022 What should I do if this is red? If gauge is Red (> 26 hours), backup jobs have stalled or B2 upload credentials failed. Re-run backup manually and check cron schedules.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 8
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "victoriametrics"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
